# Intent: The banner row, part 2 (owner asked twice that the remote bar not sit over the mouth). Every message that was drawn at the bottom of the face now goes to the banner row at the top: the Remote cue and the Remote SAY text (TB05, TC01, TC04: the exact words sticky until spoken or canceled, a long text scrolls, with the tap or stop hint first when asked first), the remote session as a violet chip (the old glyph at the top left and the bottom bar are gone), "Here I am!" and the game best score (Y04), the notices of the daily rules (T01), the volume and Wi-Fi toasts, the link looks (R03: the slashed bars with Offline, the bars with Connecting, the key with Waiting for approval), the camera-on cue (T05, now in the strip) and the captions (TA04: now the subtitle strip). New settings: captions_mode (off, subtitles by default when on, banner; the Stock style's bubble became the subtitles) and top_bar (hidden by default, or always show battery and Wi-Fi). The Wi-Fi setup hint shows as still subtitles because its name and code must stay readable; a remote say that is spoken continues as subtitles after the banner showed it first. Battery under 20 percent and Wi-Fi or hub link lost show as small glyphs in the strip; the microphone-live glyph follows the listening state. The settings table order keeps the host's 16 keys first.
# Placement: unit (settings are kept in the unit's own flash; the host copy is what the settings page shows)
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/{maipai_remote.cc,maipai_games.cc,maipai_prefs_core.h,maipai_fx.cc,maipai_fx.h,maipai_face.cc} and board/stackchan_display.{cc,h} (ours, patches TB05, Y04, TA01, TA04, F01, R03, T05)
# Check after a flash: self.prefs.get shows captions_mode banner and top_bar hidden; the Offline look, a find chirp, a volume swipe, a game best score and a remote say each appear in the top row; self.prefs.set {"captions_mode":"banner"} shows the words in the top row.

